# Build output. Trailing slashes on purpose: without one these match a *file* of the same
# name anywhere in the tree, which is the same trap documented for docs below. Left
# unanchored because every Gradle module has its own build/ directory.
.gradle/
build/
out/
.logs/
logs/

# Anchored: an unanchored `docs` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently
# swallowed the Java package ai.intellistream.datahub.api.docs — the OpenAPI response wrappers were
# written, never committed, and master stopped compiling.
#
# Narrowed further to the pitch material specifically, rather than all of /docs. Ignoring the
# whole directory meant there was nowhere in the repository to put documentation: creating
# docs/ would have silently done nothing.
/docs/pitch/
/docs/pitch.zip

# Local-only config and credentials — never commit these
**/http-client.private.env.json
**/application-dev.yml
**/application-dev.yaml
**/application-dev.properties
**/application-local.yml
**/application-local.properties
**/application-test.yml
**/application-test.yaml
**/application-test.properties
ca.cert.pem
.env
# Vault unseal key + root token emitted by scripts/vault-init.sh — never commit
vault-init.json
**/vault-init.json

# JVM crash dumps and heap dumps
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.hprof

# Editors and OS cruft. IntelliJ project files are per-developer: the run configurations that
# are worth sharing are documented in intellij-idea.md instead.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code local tooling
.claude/
